Bottom line

Yes — auto pipeline parallelism is clearly a planned but unimplemented feature. The evidence is:
- The alpa_dp solver is fully ported and exported (but has no caller in auto_parallel)
- The pipeline_shard/ module stub exists
- The manual pipeline infrastructure (schedules, stage manager, P2P comms) is mature
- The design mirrors Alpa's architecture, where inter-op PP is the outer loop wrapping intra-op TP

The intended implementation would use alpa_dp to partition layers into stages, then call autoparallelize() independently on each stage's sub-model with the assigned submesh — exactly how Alpa works.


