  How Alpa Computes compute_cost — The Missing Piece
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  The flow in Alpa (cluster_layers_and_slice_mesh in stage_construction.py)
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  cluster_layers_and_slice_mesh()
    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
    +-- get_submesh_choices()               # enumerate all (n_hosts × n_devices) shapes
    +-- get_all_submesh_autosharding_config_choices()  # enumerate TP/DP splits per submesh                                                                                                                                                         
    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
    +-- get_compute_cost()                  # ← THE OUTER PROFILING LOOP                                                                                                                                                                            
    |     for each submesh shape (mesh_id, submesh):                                                                                                                                                                                                
    |       for each possible stage (layers k..i):                                                                                                                                                                                                  
    |         run_auto_sharding_pass()      # ← runs the intra-op ILP solver (≈ ColossalAI's initialize_model)                                                                                                                                      
    |         distributed_profile_on_mesh() # actually execute on GPUs to measure real time                                                                                                                                                         
    |         → fills compute_cost[k, i, mesh_id, config_id]                                                                                                                                                                                        
    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
    +-- training_dp()  /  alpa_dp()        # DP over the filled cost table                                                                                                                                                                          
    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
    +-- parse solution → stage assignments, submesh shapes, sharding configs
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  ---             
  What get_compute_cost actually does                                                                                                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  It is not a static/analytical estimate. It:
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  1. Enumerates all (start_layer, end_layer, submesh_shape, autosharding_config) combinations                                                                                                                                                       
  2. For each combination, compiles and actually runs the stage on real GPUs using run_auto_sharding_pass() (= Alpa's intra-op ILP solver, equivalent to ColossalAI's initialize_model())                                                           
  3. Measures wall-clock time with distributed_profile_on_mesh() on actual hardware                                                                                                                                                                 
  4. Caches results to a .npy file (cached_profile_result) so the expensive profiling doesn't need to repeat                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  # from stage_profiling.py                                                                                                                                                                                                                         
  profile_results = distributed_profile_on_mesh(                                                                                                                                                                                                    
      stages, sliced_virtual_meshes, num_micro_batches, ...)
  # → actually dispatches compute to GPUs and times it                                                                                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
  Two profile modes exist:                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
  - "composition" (default): profiles merged stages (layers k+k+1+...+i together) — more accurate                                                                                                                                                   
  - "individual": profiles each layer alone then sums — faster but less accurate                                                                                                                                                                    
  
