  Bottom line     
             
  Alpa's get_compute_cost is an actual GPU profiling loop — not a formula. It physically runs each possible (stage, submesh, sharding_config) combination on hardware, times it, and fills the cost table. This is expensive but accurate. The
  result is cached so it only runs once per model architecture.                                                                                                                                                                                     
  
  ColossalAI has ported every component except this profiling orchestrator. The pipeline_shard/ module was clearly intended to hold:                                                                                                                
  1. A PyTorch-native get_compute_cost() that calls initialize_model() per stage slice on each submesh
  2. A cluster_layers_and_slice_mesh() orchestrator that wires profiling → alpa_dp → stage assignment → PipelineStageManager                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                            
  The architecture was fully designed and partially ported — execution just stopped before the pipeline-shard integration was completed.   


