  ---
  Alpa vs ColossalAI: Auto-Parallel Planning

  Yes — Alpa also supports auto planning, and it's more complete

  Alpa's top-level API is a single decorator:
  @alpa.parallelize(method=PipeshardParallel(stage_option="auto"))
  def train_step(state, batch): ...
  That one line triggers: auto layer grouping → auto stage partitioning → auto intra-op sharding → auto microbatch scheduling — the full 3D parallel plan.

  ColossalAI's equivalent is autoparallelize(), which only covers DP+TP (no PP).

